    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Ahmadis hold that Mirza Ghulam Ahmad was the promised Messiah and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a>, a prophet wholly subordinate to Muhammad, and that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> is the final dispensation, to be restored to its original form and spread by peaceful means.</li><li>The Community is led by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliph</a>, chosen by an electoral college, and its missions began abroad as early as 1913; it is described as the first Muslim missionary organisation to reach <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and other Western countries.</li><li>Many other Muslims regard the recognition of Ahmad as a prophet as heretical. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> has declared Ahmadis non-Muslims, and the Community says it has faced persecution and discrimination since 1889.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Ahmadis believe that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a> survived the cross and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> of old age while seeking the Lost Tribes of Israel, a view that departs from the mainstream Muslim belief.</p></aside>
    </section>

